</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Safety_Hoist_Beacons" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Saety Hoist Light Beacons]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(VFD_Panel_Safety_Hoist_2_Cart_OK)OTE(TC_Remote_IO:5:O.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(VFD_Panel_Safety_Hoist_2_Cart_OK)OTE(TC_Remote_IO:3:O.7);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(VFD_Panel_Safety_Hoist_1_Cart_OK)OTE(TC_Remote_IO:3:O.6);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(VFD_Panel_Safety_Hoist_1_Cart_OK)OTE(TC_Remote_IO:3:O.5);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="_00_MX101_UpperHowesMixer" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Upper Howes Mixer Specific (non Iteration) Control Logic]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[0].Output)[OTE(MX101_UpperHowesVFD:O.Start) ,OTE(MX101_UpperHowesVFD:O.Reverse) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[0].Output)OTE(MX101_UpperHowesVFD:O.Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Compute the setpoint in Hz from the setpoint in RPM  that comes in from the HMI - (SetpointHMI in RPM  * 33.33 = SP in Hz to be sent to VFD) - so 18 RPM * 33.33 = 600 = 6.00 Hz in VFD]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(MX101_UpperHowesVFD:O.FreqCommand,MX101.SP_HMI*33.333);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Take the setpoint being written to the drive and convert it to Frequency in Hz]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[DIV(MX101_UpperHowesVFD:O.FreqCommand,100,MX101.FreqHz_Real);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Read the actual drive output in Hz from the drive and scale to a decimal - so 600 = 6.00]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[DIV(MX101_UpperHowesVFD:I.OutputFreq,100,MX101.OT_Actual_Hz);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Divide the RPM value from the speed sensor by 100 and place in MX201 RPM variable]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[DIV(ZS101_RPM_Speed_UpperHowes,100,MX101.RPM);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Manual Permissives]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MX101_UpperHowesVFD:I.Ready)OTE(Device[0].PermissivesMan);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Auto Permissives]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MX101_UpperHowesVFD:I.Ready)OTE(Device[0].PermissivesAuto);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Compute the % error from SP when device is running]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[0].Output)CPT(Device[0].Error,(MX101.RPM-MX101.SP_HMI)/MX101.RPM*100);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Write 0 into % error from SP when device in not running]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[0].Output)MOV(0,Device[0].Error);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If % error above or below limits - start interlock persistance timer]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Device[0].Error,10) ,LES(Device[0].Error,-10) ]TON(Device[0].ErrorTimer,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If error persistance timer done - interlock device]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[0].ErrorTimer.DN)XIC(alwaysOFF)OTL(MX101.DevErrorInterlock);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If Mixer 101 Lid open - Interlock the mixer]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(VFD_Panel_Safety_MX101_Lid_Ok)OTL(MX101.LidInterlock);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Get the VFD status word to set no comms bit if comms gone]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(Module,MX101_UpperHowesVFD,EntryStatus,Device[0].VFDEntryStatus);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Think of the MEQ as saying:

"Ignore everything in VFDEntryStatus except these particular bits, and tell me whether those bits equal 4."]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MEQ(Device[0].VFDEntryStatus,16#0000F000,16#00004000)OTE(Device[0].VFDCommsOK);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD comms NOT ok - set the VFD comms interlock bit for Device[0] - MX101
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[0].VFDCommsOK)[OTE(MX101.VFDCommsIntlk) ,MOV(20,Device[0].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD Faulted - set the VFD faulted interlock bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MX101_UpperHowesVFD:I.Faulted)[OTE(MX101.VFDFaultIntlk) ,MOV(21,Device[0].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD Faulted - set the VFD faulted interlock bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(MX101_UpperHowesVFD:I.Ready)[OTE(MX101.VFDNotReadyIntlk) ,MOV(22,Device[0].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset interlock on all system reset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AllReset)[OTU(Device[0].Interlock) ,OTE(MX101_UpperHowesVFD:O.ClearFaults) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="_01_MX201_LowerHowesMixer" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Lower Howes Mixer Control Logic not associated with Device Iteration Logic]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[1].Output)OTE(MX201_LowerHowesVFD:O.Start);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[1].Output)OTE(MX201_LowerHowesVFD:O.Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Compute the setpoint in Hz from the setpoint in RPM  that comes in from the HMI - (SetpointHMI in RPM  * 33.33 = SP in Hz to be sent to VFD) - so 18 RPM * 33.33 = 600 = 6.00 Hz in VFD]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(MX201_LowerHowesVFD:O.FreqCommand,MX201.SP_HMI*33.333);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Take the setpoint being written to the drive and convert it to Frequency in Hz]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[DIV(MX201_LowerHowesVFD:O.FreqCommand,100,MX201.FreqHz_Real);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Read the actual drive output in Hz from the drive and scale to a decimal - so 600 = 6.00]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[DIV(MX201_LowerHowesVFD:I.OutputFreq,100,MX201.OT_Actual_Hz);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Divide the RPM value from the speed sensor by 100 and place in MX201 RPM variable]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[DIV(ZS102_RPM_Speed_LowerHowes,100,MX201.RPM);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Manual Permissives]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MX201_LowerHowesVFD:I.Ready)OTE(Device[1].PermissivesMan);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Auto Permissives]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MX201_LowerHowesVFD:I.Ready)OTE(Device[1].PermissivesAuto);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Compute the % error from SP when device is running]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[1].Output)CPT(Device[1].Error,(MX201.RPM-MX201.SP_HMI)/MX201.RPM*100);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Write 0 into % error from SP when device in not running]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[1].Output)MOV(0,Device[1].Error);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If % error above or below limits - start interlock persistance timer]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Device[1].Error,10) ,LES(Device[1].Error,-10) ]TON(Device[1].ErrorTimer,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If error persistance timer done - interlock device]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[1].ErrorTimer.DN)OTL(MX201.DevErrorInterlock);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If Mixer 101 Lid open - Interlock the mixer]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(VFD_Panel_Safety_MX1012_Lid_Ok)OTL(MX201.LidInterlock);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Get the VFD status word to set no comms bit if comms gone]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(Module,MX201_LowerHowesVFD,EntryStatus,Device[1].VFDEntryStatus);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Think of the MEQ as saying:

"Ignore everything in VFDEntryStatus except these particular bits, and tell me whether those bits equal 4."]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MEQ(Device[1].VFDEntryStatus,16#0000F000,16#00004000)OTE(Device[1].VFDCommsOK);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD comms NOT ok - set the VFD comms interlock bit for Device[0] - MX101
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[1].VFDCommsOK)[OTE(MX201.VFDCommsIntlk) ,MOV(10,Device[1].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD Faulted - set the VFD faulted interlock bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MX201_LowerHowesVFD:I.Faulted)[OTE(MX201.VFDFaultIntlk) ,MOV(21,Device[1].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD Faulted - set the VFD faulted interlock bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(MX201_LowerHowesVFD:I.Ready)[OTE(MX201.VFDNotReadyIntlk) ,MOV(22,Device[1].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset interlock on all system reset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AllReset)[OTU(Device[1].Interlock) ,OTE(MX201_LowerHowesVFD:O.ClearFaults) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="_02_GF101_Thayer1_WB_Feeder" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Thayer1 WB Feeder Control Logic (Old Limestone Feeder) - not associated with Device Iteration Logic]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Turn GF101 on / off as per the Device[2] output bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[2].Output)OTE(GF101_Write_RunStop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung copies 40 integer ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Thayer1_BS:I.Data[81],GF101_RunningLoad,20);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Write the Setpoint from the HMI to the Thayer 1 (GF101)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(GF101.SP_HMI,Thayer1_BS:O.Data[27],2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Read setpoint back from Thayer 1 (GF100)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(GF101_SetPoint,GF101.SP_READ,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Compute the % error from SP when device is running]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[2].Output)CPT(Device[2].Error,((GF101_RunningRate - GF101_SetPoint)/GF101_SetPoint) *100);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Manual  Permissives]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(Device[2].PermissivesMan);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Auto Permissives]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(Device[2].PermissivesAuto);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset interlock on all system reset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AllReset)OTU(Device[2].Interlock);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(GF101_Shutdown_ExcessDevSp)[OTL(GF101.ExcessDevInterlock) ,MOV(60,Device[2].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Get the VFD status word to set no comms bit if comms gone]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(Module,GF101_Limestone_Feeder,EntryStatus,Device[2].VFDEntryStatus);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Think of the MEQ as saying:

"Ignore everything in VFDEntryStatus except these particular bits, and tell me whether those bits equal 4."]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MEQ(Device[2].VFDEntryStatus,16#0000F000,16#00004000)OTE(Device[2].VFDCommsOK);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD comms NOT ok - set the VFD comms interlock bit for Device[0] - MX101
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[2].VFDCommsOK)[OTE(GF101.VFDCommsIntlk) ,MOV(10,Device[2].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD Faulted - set the VFD faulted interlock bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(GF101_Limestone_Feeder:I.Faulted)[OTE(GF101.VFDFaultIntlk) ,MOV(21,Device[2].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD Faulted - set the VFD faulted interlock bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(GF101_Limestone_Feeder:I.Ready)[OTE(GF101.VFDNotReadyIntlk) ,MOV(22,Device[2].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="_03_GF201_Thayer2_WB_Feeder" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Thayer2 WB Feeder Control Logic (Old - Bentonite Feeder) not associated with Device Iteration Logic]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Turn GF201 on / off as per the Device[3] output bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[3].Output)OTE(GF201_Write_RunStop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung copies 40 integer ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Thayer2_BS:I.Data[81],GF201_RunningLoad,20);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Write the Setpoint from the HMI to the Thayer 2 (GF201)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(GF201.SP_HMI,Thayer2_BS:O.Data[27],2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Read setpoint back from Thayer 1 (GF100)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(GF201_SetPoint,GF201.SP_READ,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Compute the % error from SP when device is running]]>
</Comment>
