<![CDATA[XIC(Device[3].Output)CPT(Device[3].Error,((GF201_RunningRate - GF201_SetPoint)/GF201_SetPoint) *100);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTE(Device[3].PermissivesAuto) ,OTE(Device[3].PermissivesMan) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset interlock on all system reset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AllReset)OTU(Device[3].Interlock);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(GF201_Shutdown_ExcessDevSP)[OTL(GF201.ExcessDevInterlock) ,MOV(60,Device[3].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Get the VFD status word to set no comms bit if comms gone]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(Module,GF201_Bentonite_Feeder,EntryStatus,Device[3].VFDEntryStatus);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Think of the MEQ as saying:

"Ignore everything in VFDEntryStatus except these particular bits, and tell me whether those bits equal 4."]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MEQ(Device[3].VFDEntryStatus,16#0000F000,16#00004000)OTE(Device[3].VFDCommsOK);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD comms NOT ok - set the VFD comms interlock bit for Device[0] - MX101
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[3].VFDCommsOK)[OTE(GF201.VFDCommsIntlk) ,MOV(10,Device[3].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD Faulted - set the VFD faulted interlock bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(GF201_Bentonite_Feeder:I.Faulted)[OTE(GF201.VFDFaultIntlk) ,MOV(21,Device[3].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD Faulted - set the VFD faulted interlock bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(GF201_Bentonite_Feeder:I.Ready)[OTE(GF201.VFDNotReadyIntlk) ,MOV(22,Device[3].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="_04_GF301_Small_Feeder_AcrisonLIW" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Small Feeder 1 Control via Acrison Drive SBC 2000 - not associated with Device Iteration Logic]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Turn GF201 on / off as per the Device[3] output bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[4].Output)OTE(GF301_Command_Bits.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(GF301_AlarmAck)MOV(64,GF301_Command_Bits);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(GF301_ClearCommands)MOV(0,GF301_Command_Bits);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Take the status value that comes in as a real and convert to DINT (32 BIT) to read status bits of GF103 Acrison Feeder]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(SBC2000_1_Acrison:I.Data[15],GF301.Int_Status);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This command moves a command word value that holds all the bit command for the feeder - so 1 alone starts feeder (and places other commands to 0 - like Refil to Auto, Continuous Mode, Grav Mode, Internal Mode), 0 stops feeder if you want to change other command you need to send other values here to change the command mentioned earlier - can use 0 and 1 for now - change in future if needed]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(GF301_Command_Bits,SBC2000_1_Acrison:O.Data[15]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[command to write GF103 feed rate setpoint in kg/hr to GF103 (Acrison  - Small Feeder 1)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(AcrisonFeedRateSetPoint.EN)MSG(AcrisonFeedRateSetPoint);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(SBC2000_1_Acrison:I.Data[15],GF301_IntStatus);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Manual  Permissives]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(Device[4].PermissivesMan);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Auto Permissives]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(Device[4].PermissivesAuto);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset interlock on all system reset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AllReset)OTU(Device[4].Interlock);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="_05_VF101_Medium_Feeder" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Control Logix Specific to VF101 Medium Feeder]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[5].Output)OTE(VF101_Medium_Feeder:O.Start);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[5].Output)OTE(VF101_Medium_Feeder:O.Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Compute the setpoint in Hz from the setpoint in % that comes in from the HMI - (SetpointHMI in % * 60 = SP in Hz to be sent to VFD) - so 10% speed * 60 = 600 = 6.00 Hz in VFD]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(VF101_Medium_Feeder:O.FreqCommand,VF101.SP_HMI*60);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Take the setpoint being written to the drive and convert it to Frequency in Hz]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[DIV(VF101_Medium_Feeder:O.FreqCommand,100,VF101.FreqHz_Real);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Read the actual drive output in Hz from the drive and scale to a decimal - so 600 = 6.00]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[DIV(VF101_Medium_Feeder:I.OutputFreq,100,VF101.OT_Actual_Hz);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The 3 is just an estimate for a 10:1 reducer on an 1800 rpm motor = 60 hz = 180rpm so the multipier is 3]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MUL(VF101.OT_Actual_Hz,3,VF101.RPM);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Manual  Permissives]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(Device[5].PermissivesMan);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Auto Permissives]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(Device[5].PermissivesAuto);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Get the VFD status word to set no comms bit if comms gone]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(Module,VF101_Medium_Feeder,EntryStatus,Device[5].VFDEntryStatus);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Think of the MEQ as saying:

"Ignore everything in VFDEntryStatus except these particular bits, and tell me whether those bits equal 4."]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MEQ(Device[5].VFDEntryStatus,16#0000F000,16#00004000)OTE(Device[5].VFDCommsOK);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD comms NOT ok - set the VFD comms interlock bit for Device[0] - MX101
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[5].VFDCommsOK)[OTE(VF101.VFDCommsIntlk) ,MOV(10,Device[5].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD Faulted - set the VFD faulted interlock bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(VF101_Medium_Feeder:I.Faulted)[OTE(VF101.VFDFaultIntlk) ,MOV(21,Device[5].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD Faulted - set the VFD faulted interlock bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(VF101_Medium_Feeder:I.Ready)[OTE(VF101.VFDNotReadyIntlk) ,MOV(22,Device[5].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset interlock on all system reset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AllReset)[OTU(Device[5].Interlock) ,OTE(VF101_Medium_Feeder:O.ClearFaults) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="_06_VF201_Small_Feeder_2" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Acison Small Feeder Control]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[6].Output)OTE(VF201_Small_Feeder_2:O.Start);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[6].Output)OTE(VF201_Small_Feeder_2:O.Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Compute the setpoint in Hz from the setpoint in % that comes in from the HMI - (SetpointHMI in % * 60 = SP in Hz to be sent to VFD) - so 10% speed * 60 = 600 = 6.00 Hz in VFD]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(VF201_Small_Feeder_2:O.FreqCommand,VF201.SP_HMI*60);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Take the setpoint being written to the drive and convert it to Frequency in Hz]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[DIV(VF201_Small_Feeder_2:O.FreqCommand,100,VF201.FreqHz_Real);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Read the actual drive output in Hz from the drive and scale to a decimal - so 600 = 6.00]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[DIV(VF201_Small_Feeder_2:I.OutputFreq,100,VF201.OT_Actual_Hz);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The 3 is just an estimate for a 10:1 reducer on an 1800 rpm motor = 60 hz = 180rpm so the multipier is 3]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MUL(VF201.OT_Actual_Hz,3,VF201.RPM);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Manual  Permissives]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(Device[6].PermissivesMan);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Auto Permissives]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(Device[6].PermissivesAuto);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Get the VFD status word to set no comms bit if comms gone]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(Module,VF201_Small_Feeder_2,EntryStatus,Device[6].VFDEntryStatus);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Think of the MEQ as saying:

"Ignore everything in VFDEntryStatus except these particular bits, and tell me whether those bits equal 4."]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MEQ(Device[6].VFDEntryStatus,16#0000F000,16#00004000)OTE(Device[6].VFDCommsOK);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD comms NOT ok - set the VFD comms interlock bit for Device[0] - MX101
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[6].VFDCommsOK)[OTE(VF201.VFDCommsIntlk) ,MOV(20,Device[6].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD Faulted - set the VFD faulted interlock bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(VF201_Small_Feeder_2:I.Faulted)[OTE(VF201.VFDFaultIntlk) ,MOV(21,Device[6].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If VFD Faulted - set the VFD faulted interlock bit]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(VF201_Small_Feeder_2:I.Ready)[OTE(VF201.VFDNotReadyIntlk) ,MOV(22,Device[6].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset interlock on all system reset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_AllReset)[OTU(Device[6].Interlock) ,OTE(VF201_Small_Feeder_2:O.ClearFaults) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="_07_FT103_Oil_Dosing" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Logic to control FT103 not associated with Device Iteration Logic]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When the FT103 (Device 7) Output is on - write the HMI setpoint to the flow meter to start dosing system]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[7].Output)MOV(FT103B.SP_HMI,FT103B.SP_W);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When FT103 (Device 7) output bit is OFF - write the 0 to the flow meter controller - shutting if OFF (ie not running)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[7].Output)MOV(0,FT103B.SP_W);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Take the Device error time from HMI in seconds and mulitply by 1000 to get ms and put in  device error timer preset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CPT(FT103B.HighPressureTimer.PRE,FT103B.HighPressureTime*1000) ,CPT(FT103B.HighPressureLimit_Int,FT103B.HighPressureLimit_HMI*100) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When PT103 output bit is over 40 psi - write the 0 to the flow meter controller - shutting if OFF (ie not running)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GRT(PT103_PV_RAW,FT103B.HighPressureLimit_Int)TON(FT103B.HighPressureTimer,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If error persistance timer done - interlock device]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FT103B.HighPressureTimer.DN)[OTL(FT103B.HighPressureInterlock) ,MOV(50,Device[7].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FT103B.HighPressureInterlock)MOV(0,FT103B.SP_W);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTE(Device[7].PermissivesAuto) ,OTE(Device[7].PermissivesMan) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Toggle the 8 bit of the SINT Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[1].7 to trigger reset command  for FT104 in Anybus gateway]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FT103.TotalizerReset)OTE(Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[0].0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Write to bit 0 of the SINT Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[3].0 to enable/diable the totalizer for FT103 in Anybus gateway]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FT103.TotalizerEnable)XIC(Device[7].Output)OTE(Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[3].0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Write to bit 1 of the SINT Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[6].0 to trigger the clear reset (needed before Alarm reset)
Write to bit 1 of the SINT Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[7].0 to trigger the Alarrm Reset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FT103.AlarmReset)[OTE(Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[6].0) ,OTE(Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[7].0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FT103B.AlarmReset)OTE(FT103B.AlarmResetCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If there is any alarm condition from the flow meter - set alarm bit.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(FT103B.AlarmID,0)[OTE(FT103B.Alarm) ,MOV(40,Device[7].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Compute the % error from SP when device is running]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[7].Output)CPT(Device[7].Error,(FT103B.PV_R-FT103B.SP_R)/FT103B.SP_R*100);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="_08_FT104_Water_Dosing" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[FT104 Control Logic not associated with Device Iteration Logic]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When the FT104 (Device 8) Output is on - write the HMI setpoint to the flow meter to start dosing system]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[8].Output)MOV(FT104B.SP_HMI,FT104B.SP_W);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When FT104 (Device 8) output bit is OFF - write the 0 to the flow meter controller - shutting if OFF (ie not running)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[8].Output)MOV(0,FT104B.SP_W);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Take the Device error time from HMI in seconds and mulitply by 1000 to get ms and put in  device error timer preset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CPT(FT104B.HighPressureTimer.PRE,FT104B.HighPressureTime*1000) ,CPT(FT104B.HighPressureLimit_Int,FT104B.HighPressureLimit_HMI*100) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When PT104 output bit is over 75 psi - write the 0 to the flow meter controller - shutting if OFF (ie not running)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GRT(PT104_PV_RAW,FT104B.HighPressureLimit_Int)TON(FT104B.HighPressureTimer,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If error persistance timer done - interlock device]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FT104B.HighPressureTimer.DN)[OTL(FT104B.HighPressureInterlock) ,MOV(50,Device[8].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTE(Device[8].PermissivesAuto) ,OTE(Device[8].PermissivesMan) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Toggle the 8 bit of the SINT Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[1].7 to trigger reset command  for FT104 in Anybus gateway]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FT104.TotalizerReset)OTE(Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[1].0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Write to bit 0 of the SINT Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[4].0 to enable/diable the totalizer for FT104 in Anybus gateway]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FT104.TotalizerEnable)XIC(Device[8].Output)OTE(Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[4].0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Write to bit 1 of the SINT Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[8].0 to trigger the clear reset (needed before Alarm reset)
Write to bit 1 of the SINT Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[9].0 to trigger the Alarrm Reset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FT104.AlarmReset)[OTE(Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[8].0) ,OTE(Anybus_ETH_SER:O.Data[9].0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FT104B.AlarmReset)OTE(FT104B.AlarmResetCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If there is any alarm condition from the flow meter - set alarm bit.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(FT104B.AlarmID,0)[OTE(FT104B.Alarm) ,MOV(40,Device[8].InterlockID) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Compute the % error from SP when device is running]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Device[8].Output)CPT(Device[8].Error,(FT104B.PV_R-FT104B.SP_R)/FT104B.SP_R*100);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
